From 89a33056c24f588de62fd3b713c22b6e15c934f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lij768423-svg <lij768423@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 01:59:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: do not fail-open empty held streams as HTTP 200

Empty hold timeouts and upstream idle were delivered as 200 without a
terminal SSE event, so Sub2API wrapped them as 500. Keep waiting on a
0-token hold expire, treat idle as a retryable 504 instead of client
499, cool the hanging account, and write an SSE error + DONE when the
flush path is already committed.
---
